      "side": 1,
      "message": "Current situation: these names come from the existing Java response DTOs: `MetricJson` is the package-private DTO returned by ListMetrics/GetMetric, and `FieldJson` is its nested field DTO.\n\nI used those names intentionally because the OpenAPI extraction work benefits when REST documentation entity names can be matched directly to Java response types, without a manual mapping exception.\n\nI agree that this is inconsistent with the usual REST docs `*Info` convention, and also that `FieldJson` is too generic. I’d prefer not to mix that Java rename into this documentation change, though. I can follow up with a small cleanup that renames the package-private DTOs and docs together, for example:\n\n* `MetricJson` -\u003e `MetricInfo`\n* `FieldJson` -\u003e `MetricFieldInfo`\n\nThat would keep the code/docs/OpenAPI names aligned and should be wire-compatible.",
      "parentUuid": "2b62e9b1_8e85822b",
